sequenceDiagram
%% Figure 3 — C4 Level 3 (Dynamic): one HTTP turn through the triage harness, end to end.
%% -
%% Render:
%%   mmdc -i figures/turn-lifecycle.mmd -o figures/turn-lifecycle.png
%%        -b white -s 3 -c figures/mermaid-config.json
%% -
%% This traces the request the paper describes in "One turn end to end": a POST to
%% :invoke against triage.yaml, through authentication and tenant scoping, into the
%% supervisor graph, out to a specialist and its tools, and back — emitting exactly one
%% OpenTelemetry trace.
%% -
%% Every participant here is a component that EXISTS. The previous version of this figure
%% showed an agentship-memory container, which has never been written, and depicted a
%% voice turn while the surrounding prose described this HTTP one.
  autonumber
  actor U as End user
  participant SVC as agentship-service<br/>[FastAPI /v1]
  participant ENG as agentship-langgraph<br/>[reference engine]
  participant LLM as LLM provider<br/>[via LiteLLM]
  participant TOOL as Tool or MCP server
  participant CKPT as Checkpointer<br/>[Postgres or memory]
  participant OBS as agentship-observability<br/>[OTel pipeline]

  U->>SVC: POST /v1/agents/triage:invoke
  activate SVC
  SVC->>SVC: AuthProvider resolves the caller
  Note over SVC: tenant id is bound into a contextvar —<br/>every later store read is scoped by it
  SVC->>OBS: open root span "agent triage"
  SVC->>ENG: run(spec, input, RunContext)
  activate ENG

  ENG->>CKPT: load conversation<br/>(tenant / agent / session)
  CKPT-->>ENG: prior messages

  rect rgb(236, 253, 245)
    Note over ENG,LLM: supervisor graph — one span per node
    ENG->>LLM: classify: which specialist?
    LLM-->>ENG: "billing"
    ENG->>ENG: lookup_route → billing specialist
    ENG->>LLM: dispatch: specialist answers
    LLM->>TOOL: tool call
    TOOL-->>LLM: result
    LLM-->>ENG: draft answer
    ENG->>ENG: resolve: merge specialist answers
  end

  ENG->>CKPT: checkpoint after every node
  ENG->>OBS: model + tool spans,<br/>tokens, cost, latency
  ENG-->>SVC: Result(output, resume_token?)
  deactivate ENG

  SVC->>OBS: close root span
  OBS-->>OBS: export one trace (OTLP)
  SVC-->>U: 200 with answer,<br/>session id, X-Trace-Id
  deactivate SVC

  Note over U,OBS: A paused run returns a resume token instead, and :resume<br/>continues it from the last checkpoint — over REST and over the stream alike.
